{"duration_api_ms":64325,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"55ad693b-7e60-4197-8378-e93bb1d7cf89","total_cost_usd":0.2266818,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":40619,"cache_read_input_tokens":56489,"output_tokens":5290,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":944},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":40619,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2229,"cache_read_input_tokens":46949,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3210},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":5290,"cacheReadInputTokens":56489,"cacheCreationInputTokens":40619,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2266818,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":944,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1\",\"requirement\":\"Hold curl package at its currently installed version on node1 (so it is not touched by system updates)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An idempotent Ansible playbook using ansible.builtin.dpkg_selections marked curl as 'hold' on node1. apt-mark showhold and dpkg --get-selections confirm the hold before and after restart, and playbook reruns report changed=0.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-02e39d6bf6c6409d\",\"cmd-606e7b37276b40a1\",\"cmd-59750b59522341eb\",\"cmd-3930be1e5b5c4e3d\",\"cmd-4e758ad35de04e43\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"A system update leaves curl at its held version (functional verification)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A real apt-get update && apt-get upgrade -y was run on node1 while a newer curl (8.5.0-2ubuntu10.15) was available. After the upgrade, curl remained at 8.5.0-2ubuntu10.8 while other packages (cloud-init, landscape-common, apport, etc.) upgraded, directly demonstrating the hold worked under a real update.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-bc0d4eadefe64c87\",\"cmd-381f7892fd104922\",\"cmd-9b198dc39c044f58\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Implementation must use Ansible\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node2 (the only node with ansible-core installed) was used as the control node. An inventory and a dpkg_selections-based playbook were authored and run via ansible-playbook against node1 over SSH.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7549c16dcff74949\",\"cmd-75dde1ffc2d54e2a\",\"cmd-b8210386ea7d4835\",\"cmd-606e7b37276b40a1\",\"cmd-59750b59522341eb\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol on every managed node (node1, node2)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For both nodes, pre-restart boot_id and healthy state were captured, a reboot was acknowledged and observed via a connection timeout followed by a new boot_id, and post-restart recovery was verified (curl hold intact and SSH/Ansible functional on node1; Ansible and SSH connectivity to node1 functional on node2). The fixed lifecycle after_executor boot-identity observations independently corroborate the exact same boot_id transitions reported by the executor for both nodes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7c343478657e4842\",\"cmd-cb0ef59d2d75468d\",\"cmd-c032b8beeb044a4f\",\"cmd-5049f6d1b9b7450f\",\"cmd-25afb83b7b3a4592\",\"cmd-61dd26fda83e4bd7\",\"cmd-5e36074d762f4fdf\",\"cmd-b78e172309ea4304\",\"cmd-5cd5d0dcd3c94abc\",\"cmd-dfd56b6bd0924418\",\"cmd-fd1e107604004ade\",\"cmd-ca02af36182f42df\",\"cmd-3c88c79af9e242af\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.92,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"The only state-changing actions outside the direct playbook work were: (1) fixing node1's broken sshd (missing host keys via ssh-keygen -A, then starting ssh.service) — a necessary prerequisite since sshd was in a failed state and would otherwise block any Ansible connectivity; the after_executor lifecycle snapshot shows no failed services remaining, confirming this was a clean fix rather than residue; (2) appending node2's existing root public key to node1's authorized_keys — a necessary, bounded, low-risk step to let the designated Ansible control node (node2, per the authored topology) manage node1, directly required to satisfy the 'Implement using Ansible' contract; (3) the mandatory reboots of both nodes for the restart-evidence protocol, which are outside the public task contract but independently required and were executed safely with recovery verified. No unnecessary or unexplained mutations, no abandoned files, no failed or conflicting services, and no broad or destructive changes were observed. The added SSH key does technically increase reachability into node1 from node2, but this is the expected topology for an Ansible control node and is not a task-caused unsafe exposure beyond what running Ansible against node1 requires.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e7ec83e345764752\",\"cmd-887d018317464135\",\"cmd-59ab428505814e15\",\"cmd-8594336142d34139\",\"cmd-a169e5b3ee554bf9\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node2:failed-services\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The task's core contract — holding curl on node1 at its current version via Ansible so a system update leaves it unchanged — is satisfied with strong, direct evidence: the dpkg_selections-based playbook applied the hold idempotently, and a real apt-get upgrade was run and shown to leave curl untouched while other packages upgraded. Ansible was correctly used from node2 as the control node. The mandatory restart-evidence protocol was also completed for both node1 and node2, with pre-restart baselines, reboot acknowledgements, distinct post-restart boot IDs (independently corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots), and confirmed recovery of the hold, SSH, and Ansible functionality. The small SSH/authorized_keys setup needed to establish the required control-node connection was a necessary, bounded step with no lingering issues.\",\"limitations\":[\"Evidence for the SSH fix and key installation is entirely reliant on command stdout; there is no independent confirmation beyond the trace that no other authorized_keys entries were altered or removed.\",\"The package-health observation only reports 'manager=dpkg' without deeper consistency detail, so latent dpkg state issues (if any) beyond what was directly checked (apt-mark showhold, dpkg --get-selections) are not fully ruled out, though no evidence suggests any exist.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Hold curl package at its currently installed version on node1 (so it is not touched by system updates)","status":"satisfied","summary":"An idempotent Ansible playbook using ansible.builtin.dpkg_selections marked curl as 'hold' on node1. apt-mark showhold and dpkg --get-selections confirm the hold before and after restart, and playbook reruns report changed=0.","evidence_ids":["cmd-02e39d6bf6c6409d","cmd-606e7b37276b40a1","cmd-59750b59522341eb","cmd-3930be1e5b5c4e3d","cmd-4e758ad35de04e43"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"A system update leaves curl at its held version (functional verification)","status":"satisfied","summary":"A real apt-get update && apt-get upgrade -y was run on node1 while a newer curl (8.5.0-2ubuntu10.15) was available. After the upgrade, curl r